    <string name="font_axes_info_title">Parameter axes (glyph shape)</string>
    <string name="font_axes_info_ok">Got it</string>
    <string name="font_axes_info_message">Standard axes
• Width (wdth) — Width: condensed ↔ expanded (flatter or wider sides).
• Weight (wght) — Weight: Light → Regular → Bold → Black.
• Optical Size (opsz) — Optimizes drawing for small (UI) or large (titles) sizes.
• Grade (GRAD) — Visual weight without changing advance width: denser or lighter while keeping layout.
• Slant (slnt) — Oblique slant (not a true italic).

Parametric axes (glyph shape)
• Thick stroke (XOPQ) — Thickness of vertical strokes (stems of H, I, n…).
• Thin stroke (YOPQ) — Thickness of horizontal strokes (bars of E, H, f…).
• Counter width (XTRA) — Counter width (inner gaps): tighter or more open.
• Uppercase (YTUC) — Cap height.
• Lowercase (YTLC) — x-height.
• Ascender (YTAS) — Ascender height (b, d, h, l…).
• Descender (YTDE) — Descender depth (g, p, q, y…).
• Figure height (YTFI) — Figure height / proportion (very useful for clocks).

Note: All these variations are available in full variable fonts such as Roboto Flex. On fixed fonts or fonts with fewer axes, unsupported controls are ignored.</string>
